# Collection floors, consumed by the "Assert collection is non-vacuous" and
# "Assert the run was non-vacuous" steps in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# They exist because a file whose name lacks a `test_` prefix is SILENTLY
# skipped by directory collection — that is how tests/goals_api_schema.py
# (15 assertions) went invisible to every run for months while CI stayed green.
# A bare `pytest tests/goals_api_schema.py` DID collect it, which is exactly why
# the bug was so easy to miss: the one place that named the file worked, and the
# place that would have caught it (the directory run) did not.
#
# RULES FOR MAINTAINING THESE NUMBERS
#   * Adding tests        -> raise the number it affects.
#   * Deleting tests      -> lower it, and say why in the PR. A lower number
#                            with tests removed is legitimate; a lower number
#                            with none removed is the bug this guards.
#   * Renaming/moving any file in tests/ -> re-run BOTH commands below and
#                            update this file before merging.
#
#   pytest tests/ --collect-only -q                              -> TOTAL
#   pytest tests/ --collect-only -q -m "not requires_upstream"  -> CONTRACT
#
# Ledger for the 2026-09-27 consolidation (46 -> 31 on the committed tree; 33
# in a working tree that also carries 2 uncommitted commerce tests). The drop is
# 13 DELETED duplicates, not lost coverage: tests/test_goals_contract.py asserted
# the whole documented endpoint set a THIRD time, overlapping the two
# per-concern files. Every one of its 15 test functions is accounted for:
#
#   13 removed as duplicates of an existing, equal-or-stronger assertion --
#      8 plain endpoint duplicates of test_api_schema.py (root, health, search,
#      search/fast, images, videos, news, spellcheck) and 5 Goals duplicates of
#      test_goals_api_schema.py (create, answers roadmap, get status,
#      leaderboard, quick roadmap), whose versions additionally submit REAL
#      structured answers and assert the roadmap is non-degenerate.
#    2 MOVED, not deleted: test_negation_not_from_sony and test_price_lt_parsed
#      are search-contract assertions and now live in test_api_schema.py.
#
# Keeping that third copy was the "one contract, three sources of truth" trap:
# a fix landing in one file leaves the others silently unverified, which is how
# three real contract defects rode a green master on 2026-08-24.
#
# The floors were also STALE (44 recorded while the tree actually collected 46)
# — a floor only catches shrinkage when it is correct.
#
# A third correction, and the one that proves this gate earns its keep: the
# first version of this file was derived from a tree that had 2 UNCOMMITTED
# tests in it (pending commerce-contract work from t_c7ba85d3), so it recorded
# TOTAL=33 while the committed tree collects 31. The gate failed the very first
# CI run with "collected 31, expected at least 33" — i.e. it caught a floor
# derived from the wrong tree, which is precisely the failure mode a hand-typed
# magic number invites and a recorded-from-the-committed-tree number does not.
# These numbers therefore come from `git stash`-ed HEAD, not the working tree.
#
# NOTE for whoever commits the 2 pending commerce tests: raise TOTAL to 33 and
# CONTRACT to 27, or the collection gate will (correctly) demand it.
#
# 31 = TOTAL collected by directory
TOTAL=31
# 25 = of which the CI gateway-contract run (`-m "not requires_upstream"`) must execute
CONTRACT=25
